Friday Update
* AMD amd SPWR calls in gear. Buy PTON calls* Stocks sloppy in tight range =
as earnings are in focus Stocks are thrashing around the unchanged line tod=
ay as investors balanced weaker economic data with optimism surrounding COV=
ID-19 vaccine rollouts and fiscal stimulus.The Dow Jones Industrial Average=
 eased 7.04 points, or 0.02%, to 31,423.66. The S&amp;P 500 edged up 7.45 p=
oints, or 0.19% to 3,923.83 and the Nasdaq Composite rose 27.98 points, or =
0.2%, to 14,053.75.All three key indexes have scaled record highs this week=
, partly on expectations of another $1.9 trillion stimulus package to help =
the struggling economy.Meanwhile, Walt Disney (DIS) was 0.5% lower amid a s=
lew of price target upgrades from analysts following a strong showing of it=
s Disney+ streaming service in Q4.PayPal (PYPL) rose almost 4% after the co=
mpany gave an outlook over its five-year plan at its Investor Day session. =
The rise pushed its valuation to around $346 billion, exceeding Mastercard'=
s (MA) $338 billion.On the energy front, oil prices were higher, extending =
their recent gains on bets for improving economic outlook, with US West Tex=
as Intermediate up 2.2% to $58.54 per barrel .Oil majors rose, with Exxon M=
obil (XOM) and Chevron (CVX) all higher.Among the gainers, Inovio Pharmaceu=
ticals (INO) was up 15% after Oppenheimer brokerage started coverage with a=
n outperform rating and a $35 price target. ImmunoGen (IMGN) rose 27% on be=
tter-than-expected Q4 results. HubSpot (HUBS) added 17% after Q4 results th=
at prompted a slew of price target upgrades, including from Morgan Stanley =
on growth acceleration. =E2=80=A6 On the losing side, Amicus Therapeutics (=
FOLD) sank 32% after a partial late-stage trial setback.Portfolio: We sold =
SPWR calls at first target yesterday for 25% gain. SPWR second half is down=
 slightly. AMD calls are flat. Adjust targets/stops. =E2=80=A6 We have one =
new idea for you.*CURRENT RECOMMENDATIONSSunPower Corp. (SPWR) February $48=
 calls-- Symbol: SPWR210219C00048000-- Bought on Feb. 9 at $5.50-- Sold hal=
f Feb 11 at $6.90 target for 25.4% gain-- Now trading at $5.15-- Set up to =
sell second half at new&nbsp; $8.00 lmt gtc-- Set stop at $4.90, good after=
 10:30 a.m. ET only*Advanced Micro Devices (AMD) March $95 calls-- Symbol: =
AMD210319C00095000-- Bought Feb. 10 at $4.70.-- Now trading at $4.70-- Set =
up to sell half at new $5.75 lmt gtc and half at new $7.00 lmt gtc-- Set st=
op at new $3.55 stp, good after 10:30 a.m. ET only*NEW RECOMMENDATIONPeloto=
n Interactive (PTON) March 180 calls-- Symbol: PTON210319C00180000-- Order:=
 Buy at $3.70 lmt day only-- If filled, set up to sell half at $5.20 lmt gt=
c and half at $6.60 lmt gtc-- If filled, set stop at $2.75 stp, good after =
10:30 a.m. ET only*Thanks for reading,Jon D. MarkmanAll recommendations are=
 for monthly options expiring on the third Friday of the specified month un=
